{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Or three witnesses.</b> The accepted rule is two witnesses, according to the Gaon [Saadia]. Now the Torah did not specify whether the testimony of relatives, of a woman, or of an enemy of the deceased is admissible. Some say: if two witnesses contradict two witnesses, a third decides the verdict, whether for acquittal or for conviction. Some say: two from the sages, and three from others. And we too, perforce, follow the received tradition."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:47.838805922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}